# Doom update handoff

When a Doom mod file is updated and ready to ship, copy only the changed files to the three places below. Use the same path the file has under `Mods`. Do not search the disk, FileZilla, or the repo for these locations. Do not copy to Manda. Do not use `7 Days to Die - Doom` (that install has no "Test" in the name). Do not print the password.

If the user says **Doom Work**, follow `.cursor/rules/doom-work.mdc` instead. That copies the files in Downloads into `ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone` on all four locations, including Manda.

Example file: `Mods\ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone\DoomMultiplayer.dll`

## 1. Dan folder

`C:\GitHub\7D2D-Mods\00_Support\DoomLevelsSource\UpdateForDan\ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone\DoomMultiplayer.dll`

Dan copies the contents of `UpdateForDan` into his Mods folder.

## 2. Doom Test local

`C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\7 Days to Die - Doom Test\Mods\ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone\DoomMultiplayer.dll`

## 3. Doom Test dedicated

SFTP, not FTP. Host `63.143.56.130`, port `8822`, user `aurorat`.

Remote file: `63.143.56.130_41341/Mods/ZZZ_DoomMod_Standalone/DoomMultiplayer.dll`

Password: FileZilla site named `Giggles Site` in `C:\Users\rft30\AppData\Roaming\FileZilla\sitemanager.xml`. The `<Pass>` text is plain base64. Decode it and pass it to SSH.NET `SftpClient`. Accept the host key. Do not use the old FileZilla XOR key. curl cannot do this SFTP.

After each copy, hash the destination and match it to the file you just built. A dedicated server keeps the DLL it loaded at startup, so tell the user to restart Doom Test before the change applies.
